From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:20:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] AdvancedSettings: default the audio delay step to 5 ms

A 25 ms step leaves the offset up to 12.5 ms from the measured one,
while ATSC IS-191 allows 15 ms of audio lead. Users had to set a
smaller step through advancedsettings.xml. The delay already applies
in whole milliseconds, so a 5 ms step lands exactly.
---
 xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp b/xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp
--- a/xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/settings/AdvancedSettings.cpp
@@ -0,7 +0,7 @@
   m_videoSubsDelayRange = 60;
   m_videoSubsDelayStep = 0.1f;
   m_videoAudioDelayRange = 10;
-  m_videoAudioDelayStep = 0.025f;
+  m_videoAudioDelayStep = 0.005f;
   m_videoUseTimeSeeking = true;
   m_videoSmoothPercentToTimeSeeking = true;
   m_videoTimeSeekForward = 30;
